WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:04.850
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:11.870
Today we are going to use this new AI film
director technique to reimagine videos and

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:17.050
even movies just by saying what we want to
add to it.

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:18.800
Yes, really!

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:22.400
And you will see that the results are absolute
insanity.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:27.890
Now, previous techniques are already able
to take a photo of someone, add a beard, make

00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:33.040
them young or old, but this work, this is
something else.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:34.040
Why?

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:41.640
Well, this can do the same for not only one
still image, but for an entire video.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:47.960
Just imagine how cool it would be to create
a more smiling version of an actor without

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:51.649
actually having to re-record the scene.

00:00:51.649 --> 00:00:58.440
Hold on to your papers, and look at how we
can take the original video of an Obama speech,

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:03.750
and make it a little happier by adding a smile
to his face.

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:10.190
Or even make him younger, or older.

00:01:10.190 --> 00:01:12.470
These are absolutely amazing.

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:19.900
I love the grey hair, I love the young man
hair, I love how the gestures and head turns

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:21.100
are going through.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:26.070
This looks like something straight out of
a science fiction movie.

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:27.100
Loving it.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:29.300
Now, what is the key here?

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:33.490
The key here is that this AI knows about temporal
coherence.

00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:35.500
What does that mean?

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:43.230
Well, it means that it does this in a way
when it synthesizes the second image, it remembers

00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:48.660
what it did to the first image, and takes
it into consideration.

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:51.630
That is not trivial at all.

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:56.750
And if you feel that this does not sound like
a huge deal, let’s have a look at an earlier

00:01:56.750 --> 00:02:01.640
technique that doesn’t remember what it
did a moment ago.

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:04.960
Prepare your eyes for a fair bit of flickering.

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:11.980
This is an AI-based technique from about 6
years ago that performs style transfer.

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:18.189
And when creating image 2, it completely disregards
what it did in image 1.

00:02:18.189 --> 00:02:21.120
As you see, this really isn't the way to go.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:26.629
And, with all this newfound knowledge, let’s
look at the new footage of the new AI and

00:02:26.629 --> 00:02:30.420
look at the temporal coherence together.

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:32.349
Just look at that.

00:02:32.349 --> 00:02:34.709
That is absolutely incredible.

00:02:34.709 --> 00:02:38.430
I am seeing close to perfect temporal coherence.

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:40.030
My goodness.

00:02:40.030 --> 00:02:43.480
Now, not even this technique is perfect.

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:50.080
Look, when trying it here, Mark Zuckerberg’s
hair seems to come to a life of its own.

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:56.060
I also find the mouth movements a bit weaker
than with the other results.

00:02:56.060 --> 00:03:01.299
Now, if you allow me, let me also enter the
fray.

00:03:01.299 --> 00:03:08.390
Well, this is not me, but how the AI reimagines
me as a young man.

00:03:08.390 --> 00:03:12.040
Good job little man, keep those papers coming!

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:15.439
This is incredible, I love it.

00:03:15.439 --> 00:03:18.459
And this is what I actually look like.

00:03:18.459 --> 00:03:20.690
Okay, just kidding.

00:03:20.690 --> 00:03:26.959
This is old man Károly as imagined by the
AI, who is vigorously telling you that papers

00:03:26.959 --> 00:03:30.150
were way better back in his day.

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:31.980
This is the original.

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:36.840
And this is my sister, Karolina filling in
when I am busy.

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:42.840
I would say that the temporal coherence is
weaker here, but it is understandable because

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:50.360
the AI has to do a ton of heavy lifting by
synthesizing so much more than just a smile.

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:56.159
And even with all these amazing results, so
far you have seen nothing yet.

00:03:56.159 --> 00:03:57.400
No sir.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:00.060
It can do even more.

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:05.129
If you have been holding on to your papers
so far, now, squeeze that paper, because it

00:04:05.129 --> 00:04:11.150
works not only on real humans, but, animated
characters too.

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:13.370
And just look at that.

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:21.079
We can order these characters to smile more,
be angrier, or happier.

00:04:21.079 --> 00:04:26.780
And we can even add lipstick to a virtual
character, without having to ask any of the

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:30.500
animators and modelers of this movie.

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:32.740
How cool is that?

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:38.990
And remember, we were lucky to be able to
do this to one still image just a couple papers

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:40.720
ago.

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:43.520
And now, all this, with temporal coherence.

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:49.650
And, I hope you are enjoying these results,
many of which you can only see here on Two

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:51.270
Minute Papers.

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:52.330
Nowhere else.

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:57.889
And, of course, I would like to send a huge
thank you to the authors who took time off

00:04:57.889 --> 00:05:01.370
their busy day to generate these just for
us.

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:08.230
Now, even the animated movie synthesis has
some weaker results, in my opinion, this is

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:12.110
one of them, but still, very impressive.

00:05:12.110 --> 00:05:17.830
And don’t even get me started about the
rest, these are so good!

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:23.979
And just imagine what we will be able to do
just a couple more papers down the line.

00:05:23.979 --> 00:05:25.479
My goodness.

00:05:25.479 --> 00:05:27.069
What a time to be alive!

00:05:27.069 --> 00:05:29.879
So, what would you use this for?

00:05:29.879 --> 00:05:33.259
What do you expect to happen a couple more
papers down the line?

00:05:33.259 --> 00:05:35.410
Please let me know in the comments below.

00:05:35.410 --> 00:06:22.100
I’d love to hear your thoughts.

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:25.880
Thanks for watching and for your generous
support, and I'll see you next time!

